Project: MLLANG public repo (github.com/jakeliu/mllang)
PyPI distribution: mllang-protocol
Python import path: mllang
Spec: v0.1 LOCKED (no breaking changes until v0.2 RFC)

Before passing agent state in this repo, the assistant loads bootstrap/full_session_init.md and emits MLLANG v0.1 packets per the locked spec.

Hard rules:
- Spec file (spec/MLLANG_v0.1.locked.md) is immutable outside the RFC process.
- Parser stays pure stdlib. New runtime deps require justification + go under [project.optional-dependencies] extras, not core.
- Conformance suite (conformance/run_conformance.py) and MCP end-to-end test (conformance/test_mcp_server.py) must stay green.
- Markdown-embedded output uses the summary+packet pattern: title + one-line workflow summary + fenced mllang block. Long prose only for human-authored docs.
- Telemetry is opt-in only. Library never auto-enables. Any change touching sanitize() updates docs/telemetry.md and conformance/tests/sanitize_30.jsonl.

Style:
- Default to writing no comments. Add only when WHY is non-obvious.
- Match existing terse commit-message tone.
- Honest confidence on P: slot — calibrate 0.70-0.95, never 1.00.

Out of scope:
- Token Bot internals
- Helen book pipeline
- Chrome companion extension (not open-source)

See AGENTS.md and CLAUDE.md for the full conventions. See docs/bootstrap.md for the 3-layer bootstrap setup.
